VPN Usage and Verification Guide
Steps Followed

VPN Selection

Chose a reputable free VPN service (ProtonVPN).

Created an account to enable VPN usage.

Installation

Downloaded and installed the VPN client on Windows.

Connection

Connected to a ProtonVPN server (location chosen based on availability).

VPN adapter assigned a tunnel IP (10.2.0.2 internally).

IP Address Verification

Checked IP using ipconfig and online tools.

Verified change from ISP public IP to VPN server IP.

Traffic Encryption Check

Used Wireshark to analyze packets:

Before VPN → clear DNS/HTTP requests visible.

After VPN → only encrypted WireGuard packets between client and ProtonVPN server.

Performance Test

With VPN: IP masked, but browsing slightly slower.

Without VPN: ISP IP exposed, faster browsing but no encryption.

Research on VPN Encryption & Privacy

ProtonVPN uses WireGuard/OpenVPN with AES-256 encryption.

Provides DNS leak protection and no-logs privacy policy.

